      "body": "## Summary (human-written)\n<!-- Write this yourself, not with an AI tool. 2-5 sentences: the problem, why\n     this approach, and what you checked yourself. -->\n\n## Why\nWhen a tokenizer dir has vocab.json/vocab.txt + merges.txt but no tokenizer.json, the merges loader skips every line starting with \"#\". Only the `#version` header is a comment though, so real merges like `# #` (which builds \"##\") get dropped and text with \"##\" tokenizes differently from the pretrained tokenizer.\n\n**Example.** vocab `{\"#\": 0, \"##\": 1, ...}`, merges.txt `#version: 0.2` / `# #`:\n- main: `encode(\"##\")` -> `[0, 0]`\n- this PR: `[1]`, same as `tokenizers`' own `BPE.from_file`\n\n## What changed\n- `torchtitan/components/tokenizer.py`: skip only `#version` lines, same as the `tokenizers` library does.\n\n## Testing\n- New `test_bpe_merges_starting_with_hash_are_loaded` in `tests/unit_tests/cpu/components/test_tokenizer.py`: fails on main (`[0, 0] != [1]`), passes with the fix.\n- Rest of test_tokenizer.py passes, except `test_hf_backend_renders_generation_tags`, which fails the same way on main here because `transformers` isn't installed.\n",
